    "display_name": "How Old Are You?",
    "long_instructions": "You’re building a chatbot that asks how old the user is and tells them how old they’ll be next year, but the program has two bugs.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Try running the program and see what happens.\r\n2. The first bug is that we need to convert the user’s input to an `int` before saving it in a variable. Fix the bug by converting the input to an `int`!\r\n3. The second bug is that the program is printing the wrong number. Fix this bug too!\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo convert input to an integer, you can place the call to the `input` function inside the call to the `int` function. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\nint(input(\"Pick a number: \"))\r\n```",
